{"metadata":{"accession":"PF06736","entry_id":null,"type":"family","go_terms":null,"source_database":"pfam","member_databases":null,"integrated":"IPR010617","hierarchy":null,"name":{"name":"Endosomal/lysosomal potassium channel TMEM175","short":"TMEM175"},"description":[{"text":"<p>This family represents the conserved region of transmembrane protein 175 which is an organelle-specific potassium channel responsible for potassium conductance in endosomes and lysosomes. It forms a potassium-permeable leak-like channel, which regulates luminal pH stability and is required for autophagosome-lysosome fusion. TMEM175 is the major lysosomal potassium conductance [[cite:PUB00076705],[cite:PUB00101904]]. It is present in eukaryotes, where TMEM175 has two repeats of 6-transmembrane-spanning segments, and also in prokaryotes in which it has one copy [[cite:PUB00076705],[cite:PUB00101904],[cite:PUB00097918]].</p>","llm":false,"checked":false,"updated":false}],"wikipedia":[{"title":"Transmembrane_Protein_175","extract":"<p><b>Transmembrane protein 175</b>, or <b>TMEM175</b>, is a transmembrane protein that is thought to be an endolysosomal potassium channel. It is predicted to have many orthologs across eukaryotes.</p>","thumbnail":""}],"literature":{"PUB00097918":{"PMID":32267231,"ISBN":null,"volume":"9","issue":null,"year":2020,"title":"Structural basis for ion selectivity in TMEM175 K<sup>+</sup> channels.","URL":null,"raw_pages":null,"medline_journal":"Elife","ISO_journal":"Elife","authors":["Brunner JD","Jakob RP","Schulze T","Neldner Y","Moroni A","Thiel G","Maier T","Schenck S."],"DOI_URL":null},"PUB00076705":{"PMID":26317472,"ISBN":null,"volume":"162","issue":"5","year":2015,"title":"TMEM175 Is an Organelle K(+) Channel Regulating Lysosomal Function.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"1101-12","medline_journal":"Cell","ISO_journal":"Cell","authors":["Cang C","Aranda K","Seo YJ","Gasnier B","Ren D."],"DOI_URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.08.002"},"PUB00101904":{"PMID":28723891,"ISBN":null,"volume":"547","issue":"7664","year":2017,"title":"The lysosomal potassium channel TMEM175 adopts a novel tetrameric architecture.","URL":null,"raw_pages":"472-475","medline_journal":"Nature","ISO_journal":"Nature","authors":["Lee C","Guo J","Zeng W","Kim S","She J","Cang C","Ren D","Jiang Y."],"DOI_URL":null}},"set_info":null,"overlaps_with":null,"counters":{"subfamilies":0,"domain_architectures":13,"interactions":0,"matches":7966,"pathways":0,"proteins":7171,"proteomes":4962,"sets":0,"structural_models":{"alphafold":4534},"structures":25,"taxa":8428},"entry_annotations":{"hmm":0,"logo":0,"alignment:seed":142,"alignment:full":7730},"cross_references":{},"is_llm":false,"is_reviewed_llm":false,"is_updated_llm":false,"representative_structure":null}}